WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.601
-How you doing, bud?
-I'm good.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.267
-Yes. I want to thank you for
doing "Wheel of Freestyle."

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:06.100
You go above and beyond
when you come on our show.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.400
You don't just talk to us.
You work.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.934
You're like, "Yeah, I'll do
that extra thing."

00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:11.501
I'm like, "Thank you
for always saying yes

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:12.934
and doing all of this stuff."

00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:14.667
-Every time I'm on stage with
these guys,

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:15.834
it's like a dream come true.

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:17.634
It's like totally my dream
to be here.

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:20.501
Are you kidding me?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:23.734
-Last time you came on the show,
we did a giant opening number,

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.634
"Broadway's Back."
-Yes.

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:28.100
-And we brought everyone back.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.167
But then, actually,
Broadway came back.

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.734
-Yeah.
-Congrats.

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:33.567
"Hamilton" reopened
in September.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:35.400
-Mm-hmm.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:40.200
We actually -- Tonight is our
2,000th performance on Broadway.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.200
So, thank you to everyone.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.234
-Wow!
-2,000th performance today.

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:45.601
-That's unbelievable.
-Yeah.

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:48.133
-And Freestyle Love Supreme
was back in October.

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.667
-Yeah.
-And so it's out.

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:51.467
-It's out.
Yeah, we're playing right now.

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:52.767
And it's been amazing.

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:53.901
-By the way,
congrats on the Emmy.

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:55.267
I didn't even get a chance
to say --

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:56.834
You won an Emmy for "Hamilton."
-Yeah.

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:58.868
-Yeah. Another --
-I didn't know that was a thing.

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:00.567
-No.

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:03.968
But I got to say, I respect you
for just keeping your head on,

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:08.234
because you have 30 projects out
now that are all quality stuff.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.667
Amazing stuff.

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:11.200
Tonight, you're going to
the premiere

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.167
of the new Disney movie
"Encanto."

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:14.467
-Yep.
-Which is in theaters

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:15.767
November 24th.

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:18.000
You did all the music for that.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.601
And I will say --

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.601
Was it over the summer I saw
somewhere, by the way?

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:23.267
"Moana's" soundtrack became

00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:24.801
the number-one soundtrack
of all-time.

00:01:24.801 --> 00:01:29.968
-Yes, thank you for --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:34.000
I think that's because there's
nothing scary in "Moana."

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.000
So it's just, like --

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.801
For every parent, it's like,
"Here, I have e-mails to return.

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:40.267
Like, watch 'Moana.'"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:41.634
-Yeah. It's just comfort.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.501
-"I'll be right back."
-No, it's so good.

00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:45.534
-Yeah, no, I'm really proud
of it.

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:46.834
-Did you ever think
that you'd write

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:49.601
a smash hit song for the Rock,
for Dwayne Johnson?

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:50.968
[ Laughter ]
-No.

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:52.200
What was amazing about that --

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.734
I know you have Roman Reigns on
later tonight.

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:56.501
I got to meet him backstage,
but I figured out

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:59.934
how he could sing because of
his wrestling videos.

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:02.367
He was a bad guy for a while
in the WWE.

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:04.067
And he would pull out a ukulele.

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:06.667
And he would go like
♪ Can't wait to get out of ♪

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:08.868
whatever town he was in,
and they would boo him.

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:12.167
And so I watched a super cut
of him taunting people

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:14.033
with a ukulele to find out
his vocal range.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.767
-Wow!
-Yeah.

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:17.133
-And that's how you did
"You're Welcome."

00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:18.934
-Yeah.
-Unbelievable.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:22.834
You made your directorial debut
with "Tick, tick... Boom!"

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:24.133
Congratulations.
-Thank you very much.

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:25.734
-I remember talking about this.

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:27.968
I mean, this is years
in the making.

00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:30.434
-Yeah.
-Years in the making.

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:33.968
I looked at your IMDB page,
'cause I just --

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:35.267
that's what I do to research.

00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:36.734
-Yeah. Thank you.

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:39.334
-Yeah, no problem, yeah.
Like I don't know you enough.

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:40.567
But I saw that this is not

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:43.000
your first director credit,
weirdly enough.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.033
-I know.
-Yeah.

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:46.467
-So, in the early days of IMDB,

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:49.133
you didn't need to prove
you'd made a movie.

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:53.601
And my friend Adam Rauscher
and I made a 40-minute movie

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:55.434
over the course of
three sleepovers...

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:56.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:59.968
...in 10th grade called
"Clayton's Friends."

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:01.801
It literally was a sleepover
movie with, like, my friend.

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:03.434
-Can we zoom in?
'Cause I love --

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:05.067
"Clayton's Friends."
-"Clayton's Friends."

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:06.868
-Yeah.
-I can't get it off IMDB.

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:08.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:10.767
I was 16 years old.
[ Applause ]

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:13.334
-Nope. Forever. The rest of
your life. "Clayton's Friends."

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:17.734
-It exists in two VHSes
in the world.

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:18.834
-I love that it's on there.
-Yeah.

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:20.167
-It's so good.
-Yeah.

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:22.200
-Well, "Tick, Tick... Boom!",
it's in theaters now.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.934
-It's in theaters now.

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:27.100
The amazing Tariq Trotter
is in "Tick, Tick... Boom!"

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:30.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah. Dude, they're great.

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:33.400
You were fantastic, by the way.
-Thank you.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.334
-Jonathan Larson.

00:03:35.334 --> 00:03:38.200
It's a story --
It's about Jonathan Larson.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.133
Can you tell everyone
who he was?

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:43.300
-Yeah. Jonathan Larson is
most known to the world

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:48.534
as the composer of "Rent,"
which knocked me flat

00:03:48.534 --> 00:03:50.901
when I saw it
for my 17th birthday.

00:03:50.901 --> 00:03:54.067
I was in the back row of
the Nederlander Theatre,

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:57.300
and it was the most contemporary
musical I'd ever heard.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.200
It was the most diverse cast
I'd ever seen on Broadway.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.601
It gave me hope that I could
maybe be in a Broadway show

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:05.667
because it looked like
the New York I actually live in.

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:08.934
And it was about artists sort of
struggling to survive.

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:11.701
And I knew I wanted that life
for myself.

00:04:11.701 --> 00:04:14.868
And, you know, so I became
a theater major.

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:18.300
I started writing musicals
because I saw "Rent."

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:21.300
And, you know, when I was
a senior in college --

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.701
now I'm a senior --
I'm a theater major. I did it.

00:04:23.701 --> 00:04:25.801
I followed Jonathan Larson's
advice.

00:04:25.801 --> 00:04:27.634
And I saw the off-Broadway
version of

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:30.133
"Tick, Tick... Boom!", which was
directed by Scott Schwartz

00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:34.100
and turned into an off-Broadway
musical by David Auburn,

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:37.434
who rewrote Jonathan Larson's --
an early work of Jonathan's.

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:38.734
And it was autobiographical.
-Yeah.

00:04:38.734 --> 00:04:40.701
-He wrote this show
about turning 30

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:43.200
and no one producing his work
yet.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:46.501
And it was like a sneak preview
of my 20s.

00:04:46.501 --> 00:04:50.767
It was like a personal message
that was like, "Hey, Lin.

00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:54.167
All those talented friends of
yours are gonna get real jobs."

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:55.634
-Yeah.
-"And they're going to grow up.

00:04:55.634 --> 00:04:57.667
And you're going to be
the only one banging your head

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:59.901
against the wall of
your childhood dream.

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:01.901
And, like, do you still
want to do this?

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:04.000
And the world may never notice
anything you write.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.634
Are you okay with that?"
-"Are you okay with that?"

00:05:05.634 --> 00:05:07.033
-And it was clarifying for me.

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:09.367
It was just -- I remember I had,
like, a stomachache.

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:11.601
I staggered out of the theater.

00:05:11.601 --> 00:05:14.634
And -- And it was --
it made me realize, like --

00:05:14.634 --> 00:05:16.667
It made me fully commit to,
you know...

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:18.033
-What you're doing.
-...to what I'm doing.

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:19.634
-Yeah. I want --
-I hope it --

00:05:19.634 --> 00:05:22.067
Oh, you're going to show people.
-Well, no. I won't show a clip.

00:05:22.067 --> 00:05:23.167
I want to show a clip
from the movie,

00:05:23.167 --> 00:05:24.400
but I want to talk more
about it.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.133
More with Lin-Manuel Miranda
when we come back.

